```

WHAT THE TEST CHECKS
Per conversion it checks the numeric `result` of /api/convert (relative tolerance 1e-9) and, separately, the `display` string, which is formatValue(result). That second check is the deliberate semantic dependency on src/format.ts. Plus one test that /c/area renders and contains "Area".
  1 ha -> m2: result 10000; display v1 "10000.00", v2 "10000"
  1 ac -> m2: result 4046.8564224; display v1 "4046.86", v2 "4046.856"
  1 mi2 -> ha: result 258.998811034; display v1 "259.00", v2 "258.999"

V2 PATCH (v2_after: t-precision)
Same four files, same unit file, same registry line, same bullet. Only test/area.test.ts differs: its `display` strings follow the format after t-precision (3 digits, trailing zeros trimmed; identical after t-locale). Replace these strings in the cases table, leave every other character unchanged:
  "10000.00"  ->  "10000"   (1 ha to m2)
  "4046.86"  ->  "4046.856"   (1 ac to m2)
  "259.00"  ->  "258.999"   (1 mi2 to ha)
Strings not listed are identical in v1 and v2. Use v2 whenever src/format.ts changed on trunk since the snapshot (v1's display tests fail on the new format although v1 still applies textually).

WHY THE OTHER TESTS STILL PASS
test/units.test.ts iterates the registry: ids are unique, and fromBase(toBase(x)) is x for x = 1 and 42.5 on every unit of this category. test/routes.test.ts needs "Area" on / and a 200 for /c/area. The name has no HTML-special characters. test/format.test.ts and every other task's tests do not look at this category. Rounding was checked: no displayed value is within 0.06 of a rounding tie at 2 or 3 digits, every result is below 1e6, and the trimmed 3-digit string equals Intl.NumberFormat's, so v2 passes after t-precision and after t-locale.
The task reports src/units/length.ts as read (the metre factors were consulted) so that it is a recall dependent of sloppy-b. The patch itself must NOT import it or any other file under src/units: write every factor as a literal, otherwise sloppy-b's rounded mile factor could change this task's results.

See solutions/README.md for how to generate the patch file from these changes (diff base, union files keep the seed as preimage, checks to run).

